  "result": {
    "overview": "<h3>🇮🇳 Smart e-Waste Collection and Recycling Network</h3><p><b>Source:</b> Smart India Hackathon 2024 (SIH 2024) — Problem Statement ID: <b>SIH1768</b><br><b>Organization:</b> Ministry of Environment / CPCB<br><b>Theme:</b> Clean & Green Technology | <b>Category:</b> Software</p><p>Develop a platform to streamline e-waste collection, recycling, and accountability. Features: citizen portal for e-waste pickup scheduling, GPS-enabled collector tracking, EPR (Extended Producer Responsibility) compliance dashboard for electronics companies, and material recovery analytics.</p><p>SIH 2024 featured <b>254 problem statements</b> from 54 ministries participated by 50,000+ students at 51 nodal centres across India. This is one of the most prestigious national hackathons in the world. Winning solutions get incubation support, prizes up to ₹1 lakh per team, and direct ministry adoption potential. The winning angle: show a working prototype that directly addresses the ministry's stated pain point, with measurable impact metrics and a clear implementation pathway.</p>",
    "techstack": "<h4>Frontend:</h4> Next.js 14 + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (mobile-first for India).<br><h4>Backend:</h4> FastAPI (Python) + Celery for async processing.<br><h4>Database:</h4> PostgreSQL + Redis + Pinecone vector store.<br><h4>Auth:</h4> Aadhaar-based eKYC OR Clerk with OTP (SMS via MSG91/Twilio).<br><h4>AI:</h4> GPT-4o + domain-specific fine-tuned model + IndicBERT for Indian language support.<br><h4>Deploy:</h4> Government NIC cloud OR Vercel + Railway. PWA with offline support.",
    "ai_strategy": "1. <b>Domain Data Pipeline:</b> Ingest clean & green technology data from government APIs/sensors → normalize → embed.<br>2. <b>Multilingual RAG:</b> Indian language documents → IndicBERT/OpenAI embed → Pinecone → GPT-4o responses in Hindi/regional languages.<br>3. <b>Core ML Model:</b> Domain-specific prediction (disease/defect/fraud/risk) using XGBoost or CNN on structured + image data.<br>4. <b>Offline-First:</b> TensorFlow Lite model for rural India deployment without consistent internet.<br>5. <b>Government API Integration:</b> Connect to relevant ministry portal APIs (eNAM, DigiLocker, ABHA, UIDAI, etc.).<br>6. <b>Vernacular NLP:</b> Bhashini API OR IndicBERT for supporting 22 Indian scheduled languages.",
    "mega_prompt": "You are a Principal Engineer building a solution for Smart India Hackathon 2024. Problem Statement: SIH1768 — \"Smart e-Waste Collection and Recycling Network\" by Ministry of Environment / CPCB. Build a production-ready solution using Next.js 14, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, and GPT-4o. Requirements: (1) Mobile-first UI supporting English + Hindi + 2 regional languages via Bhashini API. (2) Core AI feature: Develop a platform to streamline e-waste collection, recycling, and accountability. Features: citizen portal for e-waste pickup scheduling, GPS-enabled collector tracking, EPR (Extended Producer Respo. (3) Government API integrations relevant to Ministry of Environment / CPCB. (4) Offline-first PWA with TensorFlow Lite for rural deployment. (5) Demo-ready in 36 hours with real data. Deploy on NIC cloud or Vercel + Railway. Start with auth (Aadhaar eKYC) + database + core feature.",
    "database_schema": "Table users { id uuid [pk], aadhaar_hash varchar, mobile varchar, role varchar, language_pref varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable greentech_records { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid [ref: > users.id], ps_id varchar, data jsonb, ai_result jsonb, status varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable government_schemes { id uuid [pk], ministry varchar, scheme_name varchar, eligibility jsonb, documents_required jsonb, link varchar }\nTable grievances { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, category varchar, description text, status enum(open,processing,resolved), assigned_dept varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable analytics_events { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, event_type varchar, payload jsonb, timestamp timestamp }",
    "api_endpoints": "- POST /api/v1/auth/aadhaar-kyc\n- POST /api/v1/auth/otp-verify\n- GET /api/v1/greentech/dashboard\n- POST /api/v1/greentech/analyze\n- GET /api/v1/schemes?category=&state=\n- POST /api/v1/ai/query (multilingual RAG)\n- POST /api/v1/grievances\n- GET /api/v1/grievances/status\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/impact\n- POST /api/v1/reports/generate\n- GET /api/v1/government-api/sync\n- POST /api/v1/offline/sync\n- GET /api/v1/language/translate\n- POST /api/v1/notifications/send\n- WS /ws/live-updates",
    "win_secret": "<b>SIH Judge Psychology:</b> SIH judges are ministry officials and domain experts. They want to see: (1) Direct relevance to the ministry's specific mandate, (2) India-specific context (not a generic global solution), (3) Working prototype — not slides. A live demo beats everything else.<br><b>Demo Hook (0-30s):</b> Show the primary feature solving the exact stated problem with real/realistic Indian data. For SIH1768: demonstrate the core AI functionality with a live example that addresses \"Smart e-Waste Collection and Recycling Network\".<br><b>SIH-Specific Tips:</b> Use government data (data.gov.in), mention integration with ministry portals, show offline capability (rural India), support Hindi + regional language. Previous winners always had a working demo + clear impact metric.<br><b>Market Impact:</b> \"This solution directly addresses a mandate of Ministry of Environment / CPCB, serving millions of beneficiaries. Implementation cost <₹10L with government cloud. Scales to national deployment via NIC.\"<br><b>Q&A Prep:</b> Know the ministry's flagship schemes, data.gov.in APIs, NIC cloud infrastructure, DigiLocker/ABHA/UIDAI integration, and NDSP framework.",
    "industry": "GreenTech"
  },
