  "result": {
    "overview": "<h3>🇮🇳 AI-Powered Quality Control for Food Safety Testing</h3><p><b>Source:</b> Smart India Hackathon 2024 (SIH 2024) — Problem Statement ID: <b>SIH1775</b><br><b>Organization:</b> FSSAI / Ministry of Health<br><b>Theme:</b> Food Technology | <b>Category:</b> Software</p><p>Build an AI-assisted food quality and safety testing platform. Computer vision detects adulteration in food samples (milk, spices, oils), AI analyzes lab test results, generates FSSAI compliance reports, and tracks food supply chain from farm to retail.</p><p>SIH 2024 featured <b>254 problem statements</b> from 54 ministries participated by 50,000+ students at 51 nodal centres across India. This is one of the most prestigious national hackathons in the world. Winning solutions get incubation support, prizes up to ₹1 lakh per team, and direct ministry adoption potential. The winning angle: show a working prototype that directly addresses the ministry's stated pain point, with measurable impact metrics and a clear implementation pathway.</p>",
    "techstack": "<h4>Frontend:</h4> Next.js 14 + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (mobile-first for India).<br><h4>Backend:</h4> FastAPI (Python) + Celery for async processing.<br><h4>Database:</h4> PostgreSQL + Redis + Pinecone vector store.<br><h4>Auth:</h4> Aadhaar-based eKYC OR Clerk with OTP (SMS via MSG91/Twilio).<br><h4>AI:</h4> GPT-4o + domain-specific fine-tuned model + IndicBERT for Indian language support.<br><h4>Deploy:</h4> Government NIC cloud OR Vercel + Railway. PWA with offline support.",
    "ai_strategy": "1. <b>Domain Data Pipeline:</b> Ingest food technology data from government APIs/sensors → normalize → embed.<br>2. <b>Multilingual RAG:</b> Indian language documents → IndicBERT/OpenAI embed → Pinecone → GPT-4o responses in Hindi/regional languages.<br>3. <b>Core ML Model:</b> Domain-specific prediction (disease/defect/fraud/risk) using XGBoost or CNN on structured + image data.<br>4. <b>Offline-First:</b> TensorFlow Lite model for rural India deployment without consistent internet.<br>5. <b>Government API Integration:</b> Connect to relevant ministry portal APIs (eNAM, DigiLocker, ABHA, UIDAI, etc.).<br>6. <b>Vernacular NLP:</b> Bhashini API OR IndicBERT for supporting 22 Indian scheduled languages.",
    "mega_prompt": "You are a Principal Engineer building a solution for Smart India Hackathon 2024. Problem Statement: SIH1775 — \"AI-Powered Quality Control for Food Safety Testing\" by FSSAI / Ministry of Health. Build a production-ready solution using Next.js 14, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, and GPT-4o. Requirements: (1) Mobile-first UI supporting English + Hindi + 2 regional languages via Bhashini API. (2) Core AI feature: Build an AI-assisted food quality and safety testing platform. Computer vision detects adulteration in food samples (milk, spices, oils), AI analyzes lab test results, generates FSSAI compliance repor. (3) Government API integrations relevant to FSSAI / Ministry of Health. (4) Offline-first PWA with TensorFlow Lite for rural deployment. (5) Demo-ready in 36 hours with real data. Deploy on NIC cloud or Vercel + Railway. Start with auth (Aadhaar eKYC) + database + core feature.",
    "database_schema": "Table users { id uuid [pk], aadhaar_hash varchar, mobile varchar, role varchar, language_pref varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable foodtech_records { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid [ref: > users.id], ps_id varchar, data jsonb, ai_result jsonb, status varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable government_schemes { id uuid [pk], ministry varchar, scheme_name varchar, eligibility jsonb, documents_required jsonb, link varchar }\nTable grievances { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, category varchar, description text, status enum(open,processing,resolved), assigned_dept varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable analytics_events { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, event_type varchar, payload jsonb, timestamp timestamp }",
    "api_endpoints": "- POST /api/v1/auth/aadhaar-kyc\n- POST /api/v1/auth/otp-verify\n- GET /api/v1/foodtech/dashboard\n- POST /api/v1/foodtech/analyze\n- GET /api/v1/schemes?category=&state=\n- POST /api/v1/ai/query (multilingual RAG)\n- POST /api/v1/grievances\n- GET /api/v1/grievances/status\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/impact\n- POST /api/v1/reports/generate\n- GET /api/v1/government-api/sync\n- POST /api/v1/offline/sync\n- GET /api/v1/language/translate\n- POST /api/v1/notifications/send\n- WS /ws/live-updates",
    "win_secret": "<b>SIH Judge Psychology:</b> SIH judges are ministry officials and domain experts. They want to see: (1) Direct relevance to the ministry's specific mandate, (2) India-specific context (not a generic global solution), (3) Working prototype — not slides. A live demo beats everything else.<br><b>Demo Hook (0-30s):</b> Show the primary feature solving the exact stated problem with real/realistic Indian data. For SIH1775: demonstrate the core AI functionality with a live example that addresses \"AI-Powered Quality Control for Food Safety Testing\".<br><b>SIH-Specific Tips:</b> Use government data (data.gov.in), mention integration with ministry portals, show offline capability (rural India), support Hindi + regional language. Previous winners always had a working demo + clear impact metric.<br><b>Market Impact:</b> \"This solution directly addresses a mandate of FSSAI / Ministry of Health, serving millions of beneficiaries. Implementation cost <₹10L with government cloud. Scales to national deployment via NIC.\"<br><b>Q&A Prep:</b> Know the ministry's flagship schemes, data.gov.in APIs, NIC cloud infrastructure, DigiLocker/ABHA/UIDAI integration, and NDSP framework.",
    "industry": "FoodTech"
  },
