  "result": {
    "overview": "<h3>🚀 Flood Inundation Mapping Using SAR + AI</h3><p><b>Source:</b> ISRO Bharatiya Antariksh Hackathon (BAH) 2024 — Problem ID: <b>BAH-2024-03</b><br><b>ISRO Centre:</b> NRSC / SAC</p><p>Real-time flood extent mapping combining Sentinel-1 SAR data with hydrological models and AI change detection. Comparison with pre-flood optical imagery to quantify damage in agricultural and built-up areas.</p><p>The Bharatiya Antariksh Hackathon is India's premier space technology student competition, organized by ISRO to mark National Space Day (August 23). In 2024, <b>12 geospatial problem statements</b> were released from NRSC, PRL, NESAC, SPL, and SAC. Finalists competed in a 30-hour hackathon at NRSC Hyderabad. Winners get mentorship from ISRO scientists, internship opportunities, and certificates. The winning angle: demonstrate a working ML model on real ISRO/open satellite data with clear accuracy metrics. Judges are ISRO scientists — show technical depth and satellite domain expertise.</p>",
    "techstack": "<h4>Frontend:</h4> Next.js 14 + Tailwind + Leaflet.js / Cesium.js for geospatial visualization.<br><h4>Backend:</h4> FastAPI (Python) + GDAL + rasterio for geospatial data processing.<br><h4>Database:</h4> PostgreSQL + PostGIS + GeoTIFF file store.<br><h4>AI:</h4> PyTorch/TensorFlow — CNN/Transformer for image analysis + scikit-learn for tabular ML.<br><h4>Data Sources:</h4> ISRO Bhuvan, Copernicus Open Access Hub (Sentinel), USGS Landsat, MODIS NASA.<br><h4>Deploy:</h4> Vercel + Railway + Google Colab for model training demo.",
    "ai_strategy": "1. <b>Satellite Data Pipeline:</b> Download Sentinel/Landsat/MODIS tiles via API → reproject to WGS84 → cloud mask → patch extraction.<br>2. <b>Deep Learning Model:</b> U-Net / ResNet / Vision Transformer for semantic segmentation or classification task.<br>3. <b>Transfer Learning:</b> Pre-trained on ImageNet or SpaceNet → fine-tuned on domain-specific satellite labels.<br>4. <b>Validation:</b> Cross-validate against ground truth (field surveys, official statistics) → report F1/IoU/RMSE.<br>5. <b>Visualization:</b> Leaflet.js interactive map showing model output overlaid on satellite basemap with time slider.<br>6. <b>ISRO Data Integration:</b> BHUVAN API, Mosdac.gov.in API, NRSC Open Data Archive for authentic data.",
    "mega_prompt": "You are a Principal Remote Sensing AI Engineer. Build a solution for ISRO BAH 2024 Problem BAH-2024-03: \"Flood Inundation Mapping Using SAR + AI\". Technology stack: Python (FastAPI + PyTorch + rasterio + GDAL), Next.js 14 + Leaflet.js. Problem: Real-time flood extent mapping combining Sentinel-1 SAR data with hydrological models and AI change detection. Comparison with pre-flood optical imagery to quantify damage in agricultural and built-up areas. Requirements: (1) Data pipeline downloading from Copernicus/USGS/ISRO Bhuvan API. (2) Deep learning model (U-Net or ResNet) with >80% accuracy on validation set. (3) Interactive map visualization on Leaflet.js showing model output. (4) Comparison metrics against baseline/existing approach. (5) Model demo on real satellite data with time-series analysis. Start with data download pipeline + preprocessing + model architecture. Deploy on Vercel + Railway.",
    "database_schema": "Table satellite_datasets { id uuid [pk], source varchar, dataset_name varchar, acquisition_date date, bbox jsonb, resolution_m float, bands int, file_path varchar }\nTable model_runs { id uuid [pk], model_name varchar, dataset_id uuid [ref: > satellite_datasets.id], accuracy float, loss float, config jsonb, completed_at timestamp }\nTable predictions { id uuid [pk], model_run_id uuid, location geometry(Point,4326), predicted_class varchar, confidence float, timestamp timestamp }\nTable geospatial_layers { id uuid [pk], name varchar, geometry_type varchar, data geojson, properties jsonb, source varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable alerts { id uuid [pk], layer_id uuid, alert_type varchar, severity varchar, location geometry, description text, created_at timestamp }",
    "api_endpoints": "- GET /api/v1/datasets\n- POST /api/v1/datasets/download\n- POST /api/v1/models/run\n- GET /api/v1/models/{id}/status\n- GET /api/v1/predictions?bbox=&date=\n- GET /api/v1/layers/{id}\n- GET /api/v1/alerts\n- POST /api/v1/analysis/change-detection\n- GET /api/v1/timeseries?location=&band=\n- POST /api/v1/export/geotiff\n- GET /api/v1/bhuvan/data\n- GET /api/v1/sentinel/tiles\n- POST /api/v1/ai/classify-image\n- GET /api/v1/statistics/area\n- WS /ws/model-progress",
    "win_secret": "<b>ISRO Judge Psychology:</b> ISRO scientists care about scientific accuracy first, then engineering elegance. Frame your solution with proper remote sensing terminology (bands, indices, classification accuracy, kappa coefficient). Avoid generic \"AI\" claims — be specific about model architecture and training data.<br><b>Demo Hook (0-30s):</b> Show a before/after map on Leaflet.js — original satellite image vs. AI output for flood inundation mapping using sar + ai. Show numerical accuracy metrics prominently (F1: 0.87, IoU: 0.82).<br><b>Market Impact:</b> \"India has only X% satellite data utilization. This solution enables NRSC / SAC to process data 50x faster than manual analysis.\"<br><b>Q&A Prep:</b> Know Sentinel band combinations, NDVI/NDWI calculation, U-Net architecture, confusion matrix interpretation, and specific ISRO missions (Cartosat-3, RISAT-2B, Resourcesat-2).",
    "industry": "WaterTech"
  },
