    "overview": "<h3>🌟 Proactive Refresh: Zero-Knowledge Threshold Signature Security</h3><p><b>Source:</b> ZetaChain x TreeHacks 2025<br><b>Organization:</b> ZetaChain + Stanford</p><p>Best Real-World Crypto Hack at TreeHacks 2025. Addresses threshold signature vulnerability where shares are stagnant. Implements proactive refresh mechanism for threshold signatures to prevent long-term compromise, using ZetaChain cross-chain protocol.</p><p>This real-world hackathon challenge comes from one of the most competitive competitions in tech. Thousands of teams competed for prizes including cash, cloud credits, hardware, and career opportunities. Winning solutions combined strong technical execution with clear problem-market fit and compelling demos. The winning angle: build a working prototype that directly solves the stated problem, use the sponsor's specific technology (AWS/Google Cloud/Azure), and demonstrate measurable impact. Reference the original challenge in your presentation to show domain awareness.</p>",
