    "ai_strategy": "1. <b>Problem-Specific AI:</b> Best Real-World Crypto Hack at TreeHacks 2025. Addresses threshold signature vulnerability where shares are stagnant. Implements proactive refresh mec → GPT-4o with domain system prompt.<br>2. <b>RAG Pipeline:</b> Domain knowledge base → embed → Pinecone → relevant context retrieval.<br>3. <b>Sponsor API Integration:</b> Use sponsor-specific AI services for bonus judging points.<br>4. <b>Demo-First Architecture:</b> Build the AI feature first, then add data persistence.<br>5. <b>Impact Metrics:</b> Instrument the app to show measurable KPIs live during demo.<br>6. <b>Fallback:</b> Pre-cached responses + local computation for reliable 36-hour demo.",
    "mega_prompt": "You are building a hackathon project for: \"Proactive Refresh: Zero-Knowledge Threshold Signature Security\" from ZetaChain x TreeHacks 2025. Problem: Best Real-World Crypto Hack at TreeHacks 2025. Addresses threshold signature vulnerability where shares are stagnant. Implements proactive refresh mechanism for threshold signatures to prevent long-term compromise, using ZetaChain cross-chain protocol. Build with Next.js 14 + FastAPI + PostgreSQL + GPT-4o. Requirements: (1) Working AI feature in first 8 hours. (2) Use ZetaChain + Stanford specific APIs/SDKs for bonus points. (3) Mobile-responsive UI with smooth demo flow. (4) Quantify impact: show the metric the judges care about. (5) 2-minute demo script: hook → problem → live AI demo → impact metric → call to action. Deploy on Vercel + Railway. Prioritize demo quality over feature completeness.",
    "database_schema": "Table users { id uuid [pk], email varchar, created_at timestamp }\nTable cybersecurity_data { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, input jsonb, ai_output text, score float, created_at timestamp }\nTable demo_sessions { id uuid [pk], demo_type varchar, inputs jsonb, outputs jsonb, latency_ms int, timestamp timestamp }\nTable impact_log { id uuid [pk], metric_name varchar, value float, unit varchar, timestamp timestamp }\nTable feedback { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid, rating int, comment text, timestamp timestamp }",
    "api_endpoints": "- POST /api/v1/ai/process\n- GET /api/v1/results\n- POST /api/v1/data\n- GET /api/v1/analytics\n- POST /api/v1/demo/run\n- GET /api/v1/impact/metrics\n- POST /api/v1/feedback\n- GET /api/v1/health\n- POST /api/v1/export\n- GET /api/v1/leaderboard\n- POST /api/v1/ai/explain\n- GET /api/v1/history\n- POST /api/v1/batch\n- GET /api/v1/status\n- WS /ws/live",
    "win_secret": "<b>Judge Psychology (ZetaChain x TreeHacks 2025):</b> These judges are industry experts evaluating thousands of submissions. They make first impressions in 30 seconds — your demo hook must be visual, fast, and WOW.<br><b>Demo Hook:</b> \"Proactive Refresh: Zero-Knowledge Threshold Signature Securi\" — show the AI solving the exact problem in real time, live, no loading spinners.<br><b>Sponsor Tip:</b> Maximize use of ZetaChain + Stanford specific tools — judges from ZetaChain + Stanford reward deep platform integration.<br><b>Competition Strategy:</b> Previous winners: working demo + clear impact metric + story. No slides during live demo. Know the exact judging criteria and address each criterion explicitly in your pitch.<br><b>Q&A Prep:</b> Scalability plan, data privacy, monetization, and what makes this different from existing solutions.",
    "industry": "CyberSecurity"
