    "overview": "<h3>🏅 AI Hackathon Anti-Pattern: GPT Wrapper Penalty</h3><p><b>Pattern ID:</b> WP-020<br><b>Domain:</b> AI<br><b>Source:</b> Analyzed from real hackathon judges (journeybytes.com, hackerearth.com, pennapps criteria, treehacks rubric, imagine cup rubric, SIH evaluation)</p><p>All major AI hackathon judges (Google GenAI Exchange, MLH AI challenge, devpost AI) actively penalize pure 'ChatGPT wrapper' projects — apps that only call GPT-4 with a prompt and display results. Winning AI projects show: fine-tuning or RAG with domain data, multi-step agent reasoning, multimodal input, or genuinely novel prompting architecture. Differentiation signals: eval metrics, RAGAS scores, custom training data.</p><p>This winning pattern is distilled from analyzing hundreds of hackathon winners across major competitions. Hackathon winners are not always the most technically complex — they are the teams that best understand what judges score and optimize for demo-ability over feature completeness. The single biggest separator between 1st place and 10th place is the demo hook — the first 30 seconds that makes a judge lean forward. Apply this pattern to any AI project to significantly increase your chances.</p>",
